Z||000002||GT Bastard||06-04-2000||01:09 PM||||Just make sure you route them properly and they won't burn.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||06-04-2000||01:15 PM||||Sorry you had to go through that Haze.<BR>I got a set of ACCEL 300+ wires and also<BR>some (sets) of wire separators. JEG'S has <BR>quite a few defferent types you may want to check into some of these and a universal set<BR>of wires, and change the route of the wires<BR>or  make them longer and hold them up with the separators. This is what I did and they<BR>look really nice and neat.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000004||Big O||06-04-2000||09:57 PM||||I picked up a set of high temp fabric sleeves to put over the plug wires on my 3800 SC.  The clearance between the manifold and the firewall was so restricted that one of the plug wire kept getting burned.  The fix worked great.  It doesn't look beautiful but it's out of the way so you can't see it unless you go looking for it.  I picked them up at the local CARQUEST parts store.||||reg||1
